  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper provides a comprehensive review of emerging aviation greening technologies, outlining a phased transition pathway that includes short-term fleet retrofitting, next-generation aircraft designs by 2035, and full fleet replacement to meet the ICAO Net Zero 2050 goal. It evaluates how electrification, hydrogen propulsion, and sustainable aviation fuels must be combined across different aircraft classes and mission profiles, alongside operational, regulatory, and infrastructural enablers.",
      "why": "It establishes that achieving aviation decarbonization cannot rely on a single technological breakthrough, but instead requires a coordinated mix of propulsion technologies paired with updated certification pathways and policy strategies."
